  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "103f8474724b7447a379016bff68b4fbdc5d2378",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 490486188,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Why this change? because, you can have vlan with public IP ?",
          "author": {
            "id": 279822,
            "username": "alagoutte",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Alexis La Goutte",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a15cba6417f4d1723eb56add7099bcfd8df373dc520577958b33c37915ef231b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/alagoutte"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-21T08:33:25.943Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-21T11:48:18.891Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 85369605,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2021-05-25T03:24:45.024Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1741,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 490661380,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Because, like in the linked bug (and also #4561, #13518, and #16762), sometimes there are captures with multiple VLANs - router on a stick configurations, captures across multiple interfaces, etc.\n\nDepending a few factors (including exactly the capture setup), sometimes you want to ignore the VLAN (when doing reassembly, conversation tracking, etc.) because the destination host really is the same despite the different VLAN tags, and sometimes you want to treat the packets with the same IP addresses but different VLANs as being for different hosts. The example capture in #14356 has one where you want to ignore the VLAN tags, because in at least one case IP fragments that should be reassembled together have different VLAN tags. Imagine some weird situation where fragmentation occurs at one point, then the fragments go together through another router that then load-balances them through different interfaces on different VLANs, and then there's a router on a stick capture at that point.\n\nThe reason for treating private IP addresses (and link-local) differently by default is that our basic assumption is that with publicly assigned IP addresses the same address on different VLANs really refers to the same host (though for various reasons we may want to treat the packets separately with the strict_conversation_tracking_heuristics preference), but with private (and link-local) IP addresses the same address on different VLANs can easily refer to different hosts and the tag should be taken into account by default.\n\nIt's possible that the best solution is some kind of three way preference - the default as described above, and then \"never\" and \"always\" take the VLAN tag into account.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-21T11:48:18.800Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-21T11:54:18.838Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 85369605,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2021-05-25T03:24:45.024Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1741,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 490696505,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The current behavior is:\n\n1. ALWAYS use the VLAN tag to distinguish packets/hosts for IP defragmentation.\n\nThis patch changes it to:\n\n1. By default, use the VLAN tag for private IP addresses (where IP addresses MAY be reused) and not for public IP addresses (where IP address SHOULD NOT be reused)\n2. If the strict_conversation_tracking pref is set, ALWAYS use the VLAN tag.\n\nWhich I believe is strictly better. Perhaps the optimal solution is a three way preference that can be set to:\n\n1. By default, as above.\n2. ALWAYS use the VLAN tag to distinguish for IP defragmentation\n3. NEVER use the VLAN tag to distinguish for IP defragmentation\n\nThough we don't have a filed bug or an example capture where the latter case is preferable, I can imagine it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-21T12:31:48.355Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-21T12:32:29.278Z",
