      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 494122696,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hi,\nI can't get my head around the case where one piece of an IP fragment  has VLAN ID Y and the second fragment VLAN id X. Can someone elaborate? Otherwise I see Option 2 and 3 as the ones to implement. Unfortunately chosing 3 as default would change the behaviour of the released version but perhaps a small price to pay to launch the \"strict conversation checking\" functionality which could be expanded.\n\nThe current behaviour was implemented to solve problems with VLAN X and VLAN X fragments beeing present in the trace casing the reassembly code to think there was duplicated packets and general mayhem.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
