        {
          "id": 494176154,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There's an example capture in the linked bug #14356. I don't know for sure how that capture was obtained, but I assume the case occurs when some router R1 fragments a jumbo frame, and then later on (perhaps in another router) the fragments get transmitted across different interfaces/vlans for load balancing, and the capture is done somewhere in the middle in a router on a stick type capture (or capture on multiple interfaces.)\n\nI agree it's some odd topology going on, but someone has apparently encountered it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-26T13:31:05.191Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-26T13:31:05.191Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 85369605,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
