            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2021-05-25T03:24:49.633Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1741,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 494701639,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The current behavior makes sense in some cases, which is why the patch does leave an option to enable it. However, I do think that ultimately the reassembly code ought to be able to handle duplicated packets (better than it does now- e.g. there are issues for some of the API calls when a duplicated packet is received after the reassembly has been successfully completed), whereas not completing reassembly at all in oddball cases like this one capture is impossible to resolve without a patch similar to this.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
