    {
      "id": "4b86d7090c9e6e6fe76be6fee9c6d3a48addcfb0",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 583988012,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This is already an improvement IMO. It should be possible to reassemble IP fragments with different VLAN IDs (since VLAN IDs are irrelevant to IP fragmentation).\n\nDuplicate (private) addresses and duplicated packets in a capture are semi-pathological cases that require some kind of preference like \"stricter conversation tracking heuristics\" to disambiguate, or some other with finer granularity.",
